{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 16250180935699205745, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 638, "mtime": 1791872269.4614606, "sha256": "a2eca866a237af42b93e909afe6794c342e50c32b565b538d5ab39e289b7fcd9"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 492, "mtime": 1791872274.4811468, "sha256": "a43e3f192a9279e2647cb86c27d43e606049ddad794814b32d4b54d9df1e94d2"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/18/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/18/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running it.\nFixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so `round(x, 2)` rounds it down. `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, so `0.125` became `0.12`. Neither is the \"half up\" behaviour the docstring promises.\n\n**Change** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now converts `repr(x)` to a `Decimal` and rounds with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. `repr` gives the shortest decimal that maps back to the same float, which is the value the customer sees (`2.675`), so halves are rounded up as expected. It still returns a `float`, so callers like `add_vat` don't need any changes.\n\n**Tests:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`. It checks the halfway cases (`2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`) and some values that aren't halfway. With the old code, `round()` gives `2.67 / 1.0 / 0.12` for those three halfway cases, so the new test would have caught this. pytest isn't installed here, so I called the test functions directly with `python3`. The new tests and the existing `test_split` all pass.\n\n**Behaviour to be aware of:** negative halves now round away from zero (`-2.675 \u2192 -2.68`), which is how `Decimal`'s `ROUND_HALF_UP` works.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 8, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 214513, "requests_cache_write": 17496, "requests_cost_usd": 0.17481460000000001, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 18, "requests_output": 2218, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial18", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 35, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T06:16:59.550979+00:00